    Account the position hiding capacity per encoded object
    
    The trusted planner now keeps one position-hiding account per encoded object:
    the random tail hides a fixed number of opened positions, already spent
    listings are subtracted per object, and a main object and a mask object are
    never pooled. A unified stage list must fit every affected object's remaining
    capacity, and the first object that does not fit is named with its gap. The
    sampled answers are counted separately: each answer takes a pad at the end of
    its message's rows, and pads are not position-hiding capacity.
    
    This is the first piece of the capacity mapping; the table, range and link
    conditions and the whole-chain round budget remain the next steps.

